<section id="admin-users" class="guide-section active">

    <h1>Admin Guide: User Management</h1>
    <p>
        The User Management section allows administrators to create, manage, and maintain
        system users across the school. Users are grouped into three main roles:
        <strong>Students</strong>, <strong>Teachers</strong>, and <strong>Parents</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
        Each role has a dedicated tab with tools designed specifically for that user type.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Main User Management.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Users Page Overview</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Students</strong> – Manage all enrolled learners</li>
        <li><strong>Teachers</strong> – Manage teaching staff accounts</li>
        <li><strong>Parents</strong> – Manage parent and guardian accounts</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Each tab shows a table of users for that role, along with actions to
        create, edit, delete, or bulk upload users.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Managing Students</h2>
    <p>Student users are linked to academic structures such as classes and grade levels.</p>
    <p> <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Students User Management.png" /></p>

    <h3>Adding a Single Student</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Click <strong>Create Student</strong></li>
        <li>Fill in the required student details</li>
        <li>Assign the student to the appropriate class and academic level</li>
        <li>Save the record</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Bulk Uploading Students</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Click <strong>Bulk Upload</strong> in the Students tab</li>
        <li>Upload the provided Excel template filled with student data</li>
        <li>Preview uploaded data before confirming</li>
        <li>Fix any validation errors per row</li>
        <li>Confirm to create the student accounts</li>
    </ol>

    <hr />

    <h2>Managing Teachers</h2>
    <p>Manage all teaching staff accounts.</p>
    <p> <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Teachers User Management.png" /></p>

    <h3>Adding a Teacher</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Click <strong>Create Teacher</strong></li>
        <li>Enter personal and employment details</li>
        <li>Save the teacher profile</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Bulk Uploading Teachers</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Select <strong>Bulk Upload</strong> under the Teachers tab</li>
        <li>Upload the completed Excel template</li>
        <li>Review the preview table</li>
        <li>Resolve any errors highlighted by the system</li>
        <li>Confirm to save all valid teacher accounts</li>
    </ol>

    <hr />

    <h2>Managing Parents</h2>
    <p>Manage parent and guardian accounts linked to students.</p>
    <p> <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Parent User Management.png" /></p>

    <h3>Adding a Parent</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Click <strong>Create Parent</strong></li>
        <li>Enter parent or guardian details</li>
        <li>Link the parent to one or more students</li>
        <li>Save the account</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Bulk Uploading Parents</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Open the Parents tab</li>
        <li>Select <strong>Bulk Upload</strong></li>
        <li>Upload the completed Excel template</li>
        <li>Preview records and fix any errors</li>
        <li>Confirm to create the parent accounts</li>
    </ol>

    <hr />

    <h2>Editing and Removing Users</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Edit user details using the edit action</li>
        <li>Remove inactive users</li>
        <li>View user information from the table</li>
    </ul>

    <nav>
        <button onclick="showGuideSection('admin-terms')">Next: Term Settings →</button>
    </nav>

</section>

<section id="admin-terms" class="guide-section">

    <h1>Admin Guide: Term Settings</h1>

    <p>
        The Term Settings page allows administrators to define and manage academic terms
        used throughout the system. These dates control grading periods, report card workflows,
        and approval timelines.
    </p>

    <p>
        Each term includes start and end dates for mid-term reviews, final assessments,
        and administrative approvals.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Term Settings Overview.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Understanding Term Settings</h2>

    <p>
        A term represents a defined academic period within the school year.
        Term settings are used by teachers, deans, and principals during assessments
        and report card preparation.
    </p>

    <p>
        Each term includes the following key dates:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Mid Term Start & End</strong> – Period for mid-term assessments</li>
        <li><strong>Final Term Start & End</strong> – Period for final exams and grading</li>
        <li><strong>Dean Start & End</strong> – Review window for deans</li>
        <li><strong>Principal Start & End</strong> – Final approval window for principals</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h2>Viewing Existing Terms</h2>

    <p>
        All configured terms are displayed in a table.
        Each row shows the full timeline for a specific term.
    </p>

    <p>
        Administrators can quickly review and verify important academic dates
        from this table.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Term Settings Table.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Adding a New Term</h2>

    <p>
        To create a new academic term:
    </p>

    <ol>
        <li>Click the <strong>Add Term</strong> button</li>
        <li>Enter the term name</li>
        <li>Select all required start and end dates</li>
        <li>Save the term</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Once saved, the term becomes available for academic and reporting workflows.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Add Term Dialog.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Editing an Existing Term</h2>

    <p>
        Administrators can modify a term if dates need to be adjusted.
    </p>

    <ol>
        <li>Locate the term in the table</li>
        <li>Click the <strong>Edit</strong> button</li>
        <li>Update the necessary dates</li>
        <li>Save the changes</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Changes take effect immediately after saving.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Edit Term Dialog.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Deleting a Term</h2>

    <p>
        If a term is no longer required, it can be removed from the system.
    </p>

    <ol>
        <li>Click the <strong>Delete</strong> button next to the term</li>
        <li>Confirm the deletion when prompted</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Deleted terms are permanently removed and cannot be recovered.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Important Notes</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Ensure dates do not overlap between terms</li>
        <li>Confirm approval windows align with school policies</li>
        <li>Term settings affect report cards and grading workflows</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />
    <nav>
        <button onclick="showGuideSection('admin-users')">← Back to User Management</button>
        &nbsp;|&nbsp;
        <button onclick="showGuideSection('admin-academic-structure')">Next: Academic Structure →</button>
    </nav>

</section>

<section id="admin-academic-structure" class="guide-section">


    <h1>Admin Guide: Academic Structure</h1>

    <p>
        The Academic Structure page defines the educational levels used across the system,
        such as grades, forms, or year groups. This structure is foundational and is used
        throughout student management, class assignment, and reporting.
    </p>

    <p>
        Changes to the academic structure affect how students, classes, and assessments
        are organized.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Academic Structure Stepper.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Step 1: Review Current Structure</h2>

    <p>
        The first step displays all academic levels currently configured for the school.
        These levels are shown in their defined order.
    </p>

    <p>
        If no levels exist, the system will indicate that the academic structure
        has not yet been set up.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Academic Structure Current.png" />
    </p>

    <p>
        Review the existing levels carefully before proceeding.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Step 2: Upload Academic Structure</h2>

    <p>
        Academic levels are added to the system using an Excel template.
        This ensures consistency and prevents manual data entry errors.
    </p>

    <h3>Downloading the Template</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Click <strong>Download Template</strong></li>
        <li>Open the Excel file and enter the academic level names</li>
        <li>Ensure all required columns are filled correctly</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Academic Structure Template.png" />
    </p>

    <h3>Uploading the Completed File</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Click <strong>Upload Excel File</strong></li>
        <li>Select the completed template</li>
        <li>Wait for the system to validate the file</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Any errors found during validation will be displayed, including the row number
        and reason for the issue.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Academic Structure Upload Errors.png" />
    </p>

    <p>
        Only valid uploads can proceed to the review step.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Step 3: Review and Confirm Changes</h2>

    <p>
        Before saving, the system presents a summary of detected changes.
        Each academic level is marked with a status indicator.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>New</strong> – Level does not exist and will be added</li>
        <li><strong>Existing</strong> – Level already exists and will be skipped</li>
        <li><strong>Conflict</strong> – Level has an issue that needs attention</li>
    </ul>


    <p>
        Only new academic levels can be confirmed and saved.
    </p>

    <h3>Confirming the Structure</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Review the change summary carefully</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Confirm Additions</strong></li>
        <li>Wait for the system to complete setup</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Successfully added levels become immediately available across the system.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Important Notes</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Academic levels cannot be edited from this page once added</li>
        <li>Plan your structure carefully before uploading</li>
        <li>This structure affects students, classes, and report cards</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />
    <nav>
        <button onclick="showGuideSection('admin-terms')">← Back to Term Settings</button>
        &nbsp;|&nbsp;
        <button onclick="showGuideSection('admin-class-management')">Next: Class Management →</button>
    </nav>

</section>

<section id="admin-class-management" class="guide-section">

    <h1>Admin Guide: Class Management</h1>

    <p>
        The Class Management page allows administrators to create and manage classes
        within the school. Each class is linked to an academic level and assigned
        a responsible teacher.
    </p>

    <p>
        Classes form the foundation for student enrollment, timetables, and academic reporting.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Class Management Overview.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Creating a New Class</h2>

    <p>
        New classes are created using the form at the top of the page.
        All required details must be provided before saving.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Create Class Form.png" />
    </p>

    <h3>Required Class Information</h3>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Class Name</strong> – The official name of the class</li>
        <li><strong>Academic Level</strong> – The level the class belongs to</li>
        <li><strong>Grade Section</strong> – Section identifier (e.g. A, B, C)</li>
        <li><strong>Assigned Teacher</strong> – The teacher responsible for the class</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Saving the Class</h3>

    <ol>
        <li>Fill in all required fields</li>
        <li>Select a teacher from the search field</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Add Class</strong></li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Once saved, the class becomes immediately available in the system.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Viewing Existing Classes</h2>

    <p>
        All available classes are displayed in a table below the creation form.
        Each entry shows the assigned teacher, class name, and academic level.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Class List Table.png" />
    </p>

    <p>
        Classes are grouped by academic level for easier navigation.
    </p>

    <hr />


    <hr />

    <h2>Important Notes</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Each class must be linked to an academic level</li>
        <li>A teacher can be assigned to multiple classes if required</li>
        <li>Classes are used throughout timetables and reporting</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />
    <nav>
        <button onclick="showGuideSection('admin-academic-structure')">
            ← Back: Class Management
        </button>
        <button onclick="showGuideSection('admin-class-schedules')">
            Next: Schedule Management →
        </button>

