        </button>
 *@

    </nav>

</section>

<section id="admin-class-schedules" class="guide-section" data-role="Admin">
    <h1>Admin Guide: Class Schedules</h1>
    <p>Define school time slots, upload class schedules, and assign them to students.</p>

    <h2>1. Time Slots</h2>
    <p>Create and manage the school's time slots to structure daily lessons.</p>
    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/TimeSlots.png" />
    </p>

    <h3>Creating a Time Slot</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Enter <strong>Start Time</strong> and <strong>End Time</strong> for the slot.</li>
        <li>Give a <strong>Slot Name</strong>, e.g., "First Period".</li>
        <li>Select <strong>Slot Type</strong>: Morning, Mid-morning, Afternoon, Evening, Break, Lunch.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Register Time Slot</strong> to save it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p> <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/TimeSlotsRegister.png" /></p>

    <h2>2. Manual Schedule Upload</h2>
    <p>You can upload a class schedule using an Excel template.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Download the provided template.</li>
        <li>Fill in weekly lessons for each class.</li>
        <li>Upload the completed file using the "Upload Excel" button.</li>
    </ul>
    <p> <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/ManualUpload.png" /></p>
    <h2>3. Smart Timetable Generation</h2>
    <p>Automatically generate class timetables based on school rules, teacher availability, and preferences.</p>

    <h3>Step 1: Select Grade & Class</h3>
    <p>Choose the grade level you want to generate the timetable for.</p>
    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/SmartGen.png" />
    </p>

    <h3>Step 2: Set Preferences (Optional)</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Prefer morning slots for core subjects.</li>
        <li>Allow double periods.</li>
        <li>Spread subjects evenly across the week.</li>
    </ul>
    <p> <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/SmartGenPrefs.png" /></p>

    <h3>Step 3: Class Time Preferences & Periods</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Select time preference for each class: Flexible, Morning only, Mid-morning+.</li>
        <li>Mark core subjects.</li>
        <li>Optionally, define the number of periods per week.</li>
        <li>Set double periods if needed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/SmartGenClassPrefs.png" /></p>

    <h3>Step 4: Adjacency Rules</h3>
    <p>Define classes that should NOT follow each other to prevent schedule conflicts.</p>
    <p><img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/SmartGenAdj.png" /></p>

    <h3>Step 5: Activity Scheduling</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Set time preferences for non-academic activities.</li>
        <li>Optionally lock the activity to a specific time.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/SmartGenActivities.png" /></p>

    <h3>Step 6: Generate Timetable</h3>
    <p>Click "Generate Timetable" to auto-create a schedule for the selected grade.</p>
    <p><img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Generate.png" /></p>

    <h3>Step 7: Generated Timetable Preview</h3>
    <p>Preview the generated timetable before finalizing it.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Edit timetable if necessary.</li>
        <li>Validate the schedule for any conflicts.</li>
        <li>Click "Save Class Timetable" to finalize.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/GeneratedPreview.png" /></p>

    <h2>4. Assign Schedule to Classes</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Select Grade and Section.</li>
        <li>Load the active schedules for the selected class.</li>
        <li>Assign the schedule to all students in that class.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/GeneratedAssign.png" /></p>

    <h2>Tips & Notes</h2>
    <div class="important-note">
        <p>Always review the timetable preview before assigning to students to avoid conflicts. Locked activity slots cannot be modified manually.</p>
    </div>
    <nav class="guide-nav">
        <button onclick="showGuideSection('admin-class-management')">
            ← Back: Class Management
        </button>
        <button onclick="showGuideSection('admin-smart-timetable-editor')">
            Next: Smart Timetable Editor →
        </button>
    </nav>

</section>
<section class="guide-section" id="admin-smart-timetable-editor">

    <h1>Admin Guide: Smart Timetable Editor</h1>

    <p>
        The Smart Timetable Editor allows administrators to review, adjust, and finalize
        automatically generated timetables before they are completed and assigned.
        This editor provides full visibility of weekly schedules across all weekdays
        and time slots.
    </p>

    <p>
        The editor enforces academic rules and prevents invalid scheduling through
        built-in validation.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Smart Time Table Editor Overview.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Timetable Grid Overview</h2>

    <p>
        The timetable grid is organized by:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Rows</strong> – Time slots (start and end time)</li>
        <li><strong>Columns</strong> – Weekdays (Monday to Friday)</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Each cell represents a single scheduled slot for a specific day and time.
    </p>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Smart Time Table Editor Grid.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Locked Activity Slots</h2>

    <p>
        Some slots may be pre-filled with scheduled activities such as assemblies,
        breaks, or special events.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>These slots are <strong>locked</strong></li>
        <li>They cannot be edited, swapped, or overwritten</li>
        <li>They are visually distinguished in the timetable</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Smart Time Table Editor Locked Activity.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Available Subjects Panel</h2>

    <p>
        Below the timetable grid is the <strong>Available Subjects</strong> panel.
        This shows all subjects that still require placement.
    </p>

    <p>
        Each subject displays:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Subject name</li>
        <li>Remaining weekly periods</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Smart Time Table Editor Subjects Panel.png" />
    </p>

    <h3>Placing a Subject</h3>

    <ol>
        <li>Select a subject from the Available Subjects list</li>
        <li>Click an empty timetable slot</li>
        <li>The subject is placed automatically</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Once placed, the remaining count for that subject is updated.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Swapping Subjects</h2>

    <p>
        Subjects can be rearranged using the swap mechanism.
    </p>

    <ol>
        <li>Click the first timetable slot</li>
        <li>Click a second slot</li>
        <li>The subjects in the two slots are swapped</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        Swapping is not allowed if either slot contains a locked activity.
    </p>


    <hr />

    <h2>Validation and Error Feedback</h2>

    <p>
        Before a timetable can be completed, it must pass validation checks.
        These checks ensure academic rules and constraints are respected.
    </p>

    <p>
        When validation fails:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Invalid slots are visually highlighted</li>
        <li>Error messages are displayed below the timetable</li>
        <li>The timetable cannot be completed until issues are resolved</li>
    </ul>


    <hr />

    <h2>Action Buttons</h2>

    <p>
        The following actions are available at the bottom of the editor:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Validate Changes</strong> – Runs validation checks without finalizing</li>
        <li><strong>Complete</strong> – Finalizes the timetable</li>
        <li><strong>Cancel</strong> – Discards all changes</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/Smart Time Table Actions.png" />
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Important Notes</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Each day and time combination can contain only one subject or activity</li>
        <li>All required subjects must be fully scheduled before completion</li>
        <li>Locked activities cannot be modified</li>
        <li>Validation must pass before final submission</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />
