<section class="guide-section" id="admin-report-card-management">

    <header class="guide-header">
        <span class="guide-ribbon admin">ADMIN</span>
        <h2>Report Card Management</h2>
        <p>
            The Report Card Management page allows administrators to oversee, filter,
            and prepare student report cards while enforcing role-based approval stages.
        </p>
    </header>

    <!-- OVERVIEW -->
    <div class="guide-block">
        <h3>Overview</h3>
        <p>
            This page displays all students eligible for report card preparation.
            Access to edit a report card depends on the current approval stage
            and the logged-in user’s role.
        </p>
        <p>
            Administrators can view all students, open report cards, and prepare
            or review results when permitted by the system state.
        </p>
        <!-- Image: Report Card Management main page -->
        <p class="guide-image-placeholder">
            <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/ReportCardManagement Oveview.png" />
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- FILTERING -->
    <div class="guide-block">
        <h3>Filtering Students</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Filter by Academic Level</strong> – Narrow the list to a specific grade or level.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Filter by Class</strong> – Show students belonging to a selected class.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Filters can be combined to quickly locate a specific group of students.
        </p>
        <!-- Image: Filters -->
        <p class="guide-image-placeholder">
            <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/ReportCardManagement Oveview.png" />
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- STUDENT LIST -->
    <div class="guide-block">
        <h3>Student List</h3>
        <p>
            The table displays students with their academic level and student ID.
            Each row includes a <strong>Prepare Report Card</strong> button.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                The button is disabled if the report card is not available
                for editing at the current approval stage.
            </li>
            <li>
                Clicking the button opens the Report Card dialog.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Image: Student list -->
        <p class="guide-image-placeholder">
            <img src="/images/UserGuideImages/Admin/ReportCardManagement Table.png" />
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- REPORT CARD DIALOG -->
    <div class="guide-block">
        <h3>Preparing a Report Card</h3>
        <p>
            When a report card is opened, a dialog appears showing the student’s
            academic details and subject results.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Student information (name, grade, student ID) is shown at the top.
            </li>
            <li>
                Term start and end dates can be selected.
            </li>
            <li>
                Subjects are listed with editable scores when editing is allowed.
            </li>
            <li>
                Grades and GPA(if supported) values are calculated automatically.
            </li>
        </ul>
        @*  <!-- Image: Report Card dialog -->
        <p class="guide-image-placeholder">
